  "query_preview": "/Monday through Friday/...\nCome Monday, the upper trough over the northwest coast will \nkeep our area under a southwesterly flow on the dry side. \nTuesday through the end of the week will generally see the \nreturn of hotter conditions, as the strong high pressure ridge \noff the Great Basin builds back in over the entire western \nCONUS. This ridging pattern will still allow some monsoonal \nmoisture to reach south-central Idaho around midweek, favoring a\nslight chance of afternoon thunderstorms mainly near the Magic\nValley and the Idaho-Nevada border. Otherwise, areas will \ngenerally be warm, dry, and breezy throughout the extended \nforecast.",
